// Layer_Orchestration_Infra — Orchestration and Infrastructure Layer (layer 1 of 9)
// Manual render: https://app.eraser.io > Diagram-as-code (cloud architecture).
//   Create a NEW canvas named "Layer_Orchestration_Infra".
// Export the PNG to materials/reports/figures/Layer_Orchestration_Infra.png
// Reference: subsec:lapisan-infra (Section IV.3, sec:arsitektur-terintegrasi); tool
//   detail for the layer on row 1 of tab:layanan_industri, detailing the same group
//   in Figure fig:integrate-service. Included as fig:layer-orkestrasi-infra.
// Focus: the k3s/Kubernetes orchestration plane, autoscaling (HPA + VPA + KEDA
//   with metrics-server), the Kueue queue, and cert-manager. The GitOps chain is now
//   its own layer (Layer_GitOps_CD); security is in Layer_Security.
// Icons: the kubernetes logo from docs.eraser.io/docs/icons (checked 2026-07-11),
//   the rest use generic icons.
// Rendering MUST be horizontal (direction right), at most two node rows per group,
//   without \rotatebox in LaTeX.
// Layer grounding: the group label carries its source category (najafabadi2024analysis),
//   namely infrastructure and supporting services.
// Implementation check: k3s/Kubernetes + HPA primitives, common/metrics-server,
//   observability/vertical-pod-autoscaler, common/keda, common/kueue,
//   common/cert-manager.

direction right

// Configuration change source (boundary)
GitOps and Continuous Delivery Layer [icon: git-branch, color: blue, label: "GitOps and Continuous Delivery Layer"]

// Orchestration and Infrastructure Layer
Orchestration and Infrastructure Layer [icon: kubernetes, color: blue, label: "Orchestration and Infrastructure Layer (infrastructure and supporting services)"] {
  Kubernetes [icon: kubernetes, label: "Kubernetes (k3s control plane)"]
  metrics-server [icon: activity, label: "metrics-server"]
  Autoscaler [icon: trending-up, label: "HPA + VPA + KEDA"]
  Kueue [icon: list, label: "Kueue (job queue)"]
  cert-manager [icon: award, label: "cert-manager (TLS)"]
}

// Workloads that are run (boundary)
Platform Workload [icon: layers, color: gray, label: "Platform Workload (eight other layers)"]

// Orchestration and scaling flow
GitOps and Continuous Delivery Layer > Kubernetes: declarative sync
Kubernetes > Platform Workload: runs workloads
metrics-server > Autoscaler: metric signals
Autoscaler > Platform Workload: replica and resource scaling
Kueue > Platform Workload: quota-based job admission
cert-manager > Platform Workload: TLS certificates
